# Library lexicon (direction)

North star: household **library** — Hall, shelves, card catalog, reading room, living lamp.
Presence · atmosphere · recognition · ceremony · warm honesty.

## Locked vocabulary (Sprint 4.1+)

| Prefer | Avoid in **new** copy |
|--------|------------------------|
| **Holds desk** | Bagging area / bagging (supermarket) |
| **Hold slip** | Generic “ticket” in member-facing chrome when Hold is meant |
| **Library card** | Profile (as the member surface name) |
| **Shelving** | Settings “Bagging” |
| Hall / shelves / lamp / Find / Ask the house | KPI dashboards, badge piles, purple SaaS glow |

- **Labels-first** — user-visible strings drive Playwright asserts and HELP glossary; routes may stay (`/review`) while labels move.
- Hash migrate when ready: `#bagging` → `#shelving` with a legacy hash map — do not rename routes in a lexicon-only pass.
- Single-writer on `frontend/src/copy.js` during lexicon sprints ([major-builds.mdc](major-builds.mdc)).

## Anti-patterns

- Supermarket “bagging,” gamification / streaks / badge piles
- Motion that ignores `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Theater / Plex / kiosk language copied from Projectionist

Until the lexicon sprint lands, do not mass-rewrite strings mid-feature unless the user asks — but **never introduce new bagging/Profile-as-card copy** when adding surfaces.
